.wrangler
# NOT anchored to the root on purpose: `svelte-kit sync` writes a `.svelte-kit/` next to whatever
# directory it was started from, so stray copies appear inside `src/` whenever a tool runs from
# there. With `/.svelte-kit` those would have been committed.
.svelte-kit
/build

